  "tutorial_example_entry": {
    "lesson_index": 5,
    "lesson_title": "Harmonic Index $k$",
    "lesson_core_move": "Interpret each positive integer harmonic index $k$ as the label that pairs $a_k$ and $b_k$ with the $k$th harmonic frequency $k\\omega_0$ in a trigonometric Fourier series.",
    "section_count": 5,
    "sections": [
      {
        "lesson_index": 5,
        "lesson_title": "Harmonic Index $k$",
        "section_index": 1,
        "section_title": "Introduction to Harmonic Index $k$",
        "step_type": "tutorial",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "tutorial_content": {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In the trigonometric Fourier series, $k$ is the positive integer harmonic index. It is the label that tells you which harmonic pair you are reading, not a separate quantity to solve for.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "x(t)=\\frac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}\\big[a_k\\cos(k\\omega_0 t)+b_k\\sin(k\\omega_0 t)\\big]",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The template starts with the DC term $a_0/2$ and then uses each positive integer $k$ to label a cosine-sine pair. The same $k$ appears in the subscripts $a_k$ and $b_k$ and in the frequency $k\\omega_0$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_1\\cos(\\omega_0 t)+b_1\\sin(\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Start with $k=1$: the first harmonic pair is $a_1\\cos(\\omega_0 t)+b_1\\sin(\\omega_0 t)$. The same index $1$ appears in both subscripts and in the frequency multiplier $\\omega_0$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_2\\cos(2\\omega_0 t)+b_2\\sin(2\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Then $k=2$ gives $a_2\\cos(2\\omega_0 t)+b_2\\sin(2\\omega_0 t)$, and the pattern continues for $k=3,4,\\dots$. Read each positive integer $k$ as the label on both coefficients and the matching frequency.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 5,
        "lesson_title": "Harmonic Index $k$",
        "section_index": 2,
        "section_title": "Matching $k$ to the Harmonic Frequency $k\\omega_0$",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "For the harmonic index $k=4$, write the harmonic frequency that appears in the corresponding cosine and sine terms.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is the positive integer harmonic index. Here the index is $k=4$, so the task is to keep that same index and read the matching frequency label.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "k\\omega_0",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Substitute $k=4$ into the pattern $k\\omega_0$. The fourth harmonic frequency is $4\\omega_0$, and that same multiplier appears in both the cosine and sine terms.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_4\\cos(4\\omega_0 t)+b_4\\sin(4\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "So the harmonic frequency paired with $k=4$ is $4\\omega_0$. The index stays fixed while you read the harmonic terms.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 5,
        "lesson_title": "Harmonic Index $k$",
        "section_index": 3,
        "section_title": "Pairing $a_k$ and $b_k$ with the Same Harmonic Index",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "For $k=3$, write the cosine term and the sine term that share that harmonic index.",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is $k=3$. Keep the same harmonic index on both coefficients and on the frequency factor.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "a_3\\cos(3\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cosine term uses coefficient $a_3$ and the harmonic frequency factor $3\\omega_0 t$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "b_3\\sin(3\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The sine term uses coefficient $b_3$ and the same harmonic frequency factor $3\\omega_0 t$. The paired terms are $a_3\\cos(3\\omega_0 t)$ and $b_3\\sin(3\\omega_0 t)$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 5,
        "lesson_title": "Harmonic Index $k$",
        "section_index": 4,
        "section_title": "Identifying the Harmonic Index from a Trigonometric Term",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "A term appears as $b_6\\sin(6\\omega_0 t)$. What harmonic index $k$ labels it?",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The cue is the shared integer in the subscript and the frequency multiplier. Read that integer directly as the harmonic index.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "b_6\\sin(6\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The coefficient subscript is $6$, and the frequency factor is also $6\\omega_0 t$. Those two labels match, so the harmonic index is $k=6$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "k=6",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "This term is labeled by $k=6$ whether it is written with a sine or cosine factor.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "lesson_index": 5,
        "lesson_title": "Harmonic Index $k$",
        "section_index": 5,
        "section_title": "Reading Harmonic Indexes in a Partial Fourier Series",
        "step_type": "example",
        "content_mode": "symbolic-only",
        "image_slots": [],
        "example_content": {
          "example_prompt": "Given $x(t)=\\frac{a_0}{2}+a_1\\cos(\\omega_0 t)+b_1\\sin(\\omega_0 t)+a_4\\cos(4\\omega_0 t)+b_4\\sin(4\\omega_0 t)+a_6\\cos(6\\omega_0 t)+b_6\\sin(6\\omega_0 t)$, which positive harmonic indexes appear?",
          "explanation_blocks": [
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Scan the series term by term. Ignore the DC term $a_0/2$ and read the integer label from each harmonic pair.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "x(t)=\\frac{a_0}{2}+a_1\\cos(\\omega_0 t)+b_1\\sin(\\omega_0 t)+a_4\\cos(4\\omega_0 t)+b_4\\sin(4\\omega_0 t)+a_6\\cos(6\\omega_0 t)+b_6\\sin(6\\omega_0 t)",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The first harmonic pair gives $k=1$, the next gives $k=4$, and the last gives $k=6$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "display-math",
              "text": "",
              "latex": "\\{1,4,6\\}",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            },
            {
              "block_type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The distinct positive harmonic indexes that appear are $1$, $4$, and $6$.",
              "latex": "",
              "image_slot_id": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
